{
  "$comment": [
    "Every capability the parity ledger grades implemented or sdk-verified names a",
    "witness here, and scripts/check_witnesses.py fails CI when a witness stops",
    "existing. The ledger's prose already describes the evidence; this file makes",
    "the claim MACHINE-CHECKABLE, which is the family's core discipline: a green",
    "row whose test was renamed or deleted is a lie the reader cannot see.",
    "",
    "Witness kinds:",
    "  go:TestName  a Go test in this repo using OUR client; asserted to exist",
    "  sdk:TestName Microsoft's own client (armapimanagement) does the talking",
    "  ci:job-id    a CI job name in .github/workflows; asserted to still exist",
    "",
    "'partial' and 'planned' rows are deliberately NOT required to carry a witness",
    "\u2014 they claim nothing yet. The checker only holds the green rows to account.",
    "",
    "Azure differential evidence is a THIRD tier this family has nowhere else: it",
    "is prepared (e2e/differential) but pending an authorized live run, so no row",
    "may cite it as a witness until that run happens. The ledger's prose says so",
    "per row; this manifest deliberately cites only what runs today."
  ],
